Operator: 'crack tn36 L6's routing and solve it.' DONE.

THE MECHANIC: L6 is a MAZE whose shortest collision-free path is 8 moves (left,
up x5, right x2) -- but a program has only 6 slots, and the Manhattan distance is
exactly 6, so a single-run detour can't fit. The solution is the CHECKPOINT
mechanic (wgzwawbgew at (49,20),(53,28),(53,4)): a run that ENDS on a checkpoint
advances the object's BASE (mnvoffrbex tn36.py:2379), so progress carries across
runs (a failed non-checkpoint run resets to base).

SOLVER UPGRADE: when the single-run ordering search can't win, fall back to a
MULTI-RUN planner -- read the object box + obstacle boxes + checkpoints from
internal state, BFS a path start->checkpoint(s)->target with each leg <= n moves,
and run the legs in sequence. L6: leg1 [2,2,2,2,33,33] -> checkpoint (49,20),
leg2 [1,1,33,33,33,1] -> target (37,8). A level's 'solution' is now a LIST of runs.
Reproduces L1-L6 (reproduced=True claimed_level=6, 74 clicks). Registry: tn36
levels_reproduced 5->6, reproducible_total 20->21.

L7 frontier: another maze the position-only multi-run planner doesn't yet crack
(likely a transform needed DURING a maze leg). Logged.
